  "post_measurement": {
    "changes": [
      "The landing rebase retains unrelated new main models and crate inventory; the quiet after sample was taken before that rebase.",
      "The first affected gate caught the obsolete one-reply capacity assertion. Correct it to require eight capture reserves plus one ordinary reply, refuse a tenth maximum frame, and include transport tests in the focused Make target. This changes no measured production behavior.",
      "The complete first affected test gate also found erased typed provider-down admission and missing async history diagnostic cursor updates. Preserve the error before admission, restore monotonic diagnostic cursors, and retain existing park/up-resume behavior. The actual four-seat exact-screen and down/up process witnesses now pass.",
      "A new final quiet sample was taken after the landing rebase and both implementation corrections, on the exact production source retained for the next landing attempt. Its actual report start load1 is 2.66845703125; 967 real PTYs/50 watched; no non-timing fixture failures. One after sample is compared with the three-run baseline medians.",
      "The second complete affected gate failed only the old raw-RPC eight-page ratio: a watched parser may be pending while backgrounds independently finish reads. Under the operator concurrency amendment, keep the exact 3:1 runnable scheduling-turn/eight-turn check and finite SeatFairness model; rename the real process witness to prove watched-tail publication inside its fixed page budget and exact serial Screens. Already admitted parsing may finish while further reads stay closed at that budget. Explicitly amend watched-replay-priority and the ICD instead of restoring a shared completion barrier. No ingestion implementation changed after the final quiet measurement; later unrelated main changes are unmeasured."
    ],
